# Board games

- Code used by more than one game lives in `src/features/board-game-shared/`
  (API wrappers, `GameError`, i18n, theme, UI, player components). One game
  must not import another game's folder; move shared code there instead.
- Room APIs (`/api/spy`, `/api/cheese-thief`, `/api/ma-soi`) use
  `board-game-shared/lib/apiUtils.ts`. Services throw
  `new GameError('CODE', status, params)`; the client translates the code.
  Admin test-room APIs use `@/lib/apiUtils` and `AppError`. Import each class
  by its own name; never alias one as the other.
- Every user-facing string has Vietnamese and English entries in
  `board-game-shared/lib/i18n/messages/`. Add both.
- Wrap public room routes that take a room code with `withPublicRoomGuard`, so
  admin test rooms stay private.
- Rooms are MongoDB documents (`models/`) that several players change at once.
  Change a room through the service helper (`mutateGame` or `mutateRoom`): it
  bumps `version` and retries on a version conflict. Do not add another
  `save()` path that skips it.
- Tests: rules in `*.unit.test.ts`, services in `*.integration.test.ts`
  (MongoDB Memory Server), and `e2e/board-game-*.spec.ts` in CI.
